  data: {
    LLM: "Know your poker hand rankings thoroughly. Knock when you have at least a strong pair or better, especially if few cards have been drawn from the stock.\n\nWatch the discard pile carefully. If you see high cards being discarded, it suggests opponents are building specific hands. If you see low cards discarded, opponents may be aiming for straights or flushes.\n\nTiming your knock is critical. Knock early with a decent hand if you think opponents haven't had time to improve. Wait longer if you have a very strong hand and want to lure opponents into staying in. Consider the pot size - a larger pot justifies knocking with a slightly weaker hand.",
    Player: "Know your poker hand rankings thoroughly. Knock when you have at least a strong pair or better, especially if few cards have been drawn from the stock.\n\nWatch the discard pile carefully. If you see high cards being discarded, it suggests opponents are building specific hands. If you see low cards discarded, opponents may be aiming for straights or flushes.\n\nTiming your knock is critical. Knock early with a decent hand if you think opponents haven't had time to improve. Wait longer if you have a very strong hand and want to lure opponents into staying in. Consider the pot size - a larger pot justifies knocking with a slightly weaker hand.",
