    advanced: "Timing your knock is critical. Knock early with a decent hand if you think opponents haven't had time to improve. Wait longer if you have a very strong hand and want to lure opponents into staying in. Consider the pot size - a larger pot justifies knocking with a slightly weaker hand.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Don't be afraid to fold after a knock if your hand is weak - losing 1 chip is better than losing 2 plus the chance at the pot.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "If you draw from the discard pile, you're revealing information about what you're collecting. Use the stock pile for secrecy.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "The player who knocked has an advantage in knowing exactly when play ends - use this if you're the knocker.",
